# Line endings (ADR 0009: the maintainer works on Windows with core.autocrlf).
#
# Text files are checked out with LF on every platform, so gofmt, bash and
# go:embed see the same bytes on Windows as CI does on Linux.
#
# "auto" leaves a file alone that is already stored with CRLF (legacy configs
# and docs); Go files are always stored and checked out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.png binary
